  "instance_name": "trump_administration",
  "label": "Trump Administration",
  "description": "The phrase 'Trump's America' refers to the political and social environment during the presidency of Donald Trump (2017-2021), which was marked by a hardline immigration policy, including the construction of the U.S.-Mexico border wall, stricter border enforcement, and rhetoric that often targeted immigrants, particularly those from Latin America. The meme uses this reference to imply that Latinos are motivated by a perceived threat or opportunity under Trump's policies.",
